-- E01-T02a: the two trigram indexes on patients go, with pg_trgm, which migration 0002 created for
-- them alone (owner, D-096). Under Row-Level Security the app's search can never use them: an index
-- serves only leakproof operators, and LIKE, ILIKE and pg_trgm's are not. The search reads the
-- clinic's patients through the clinic's own key instead. The two DROP INDEX statements are
-- generated by drizzle-kit from src/modules/patients/schema.ts; DROP EXTENSION is hand-written.
DROP INDEX "patients_full_name_trgm_idx";--> statement-breakpoint
DROP INDEX "patients_phone_e164_trgm_idx";--> statement-breakpoint
-- Nothing else uses pg_trgm. Without IF EXISTS: a database without it is not one these migrations
-- built, and the migration should say so.
DROP EXTENSION pg_trgm;
